    <ul>
        <li><strong>Authentication</strong>: ASP.NET Core Identity (cookie). Optional TOTP two-factor. See <a href="/docs/system/accounts">Accounts, roles &amp; whitelisting</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Authorisation</strong>: permission policies checked against the database on every request, plus a few role-name checks.</li>
        <li><strong>Secrets</strong>: Azure Key Vault. Nothing secret should be in <code>appsettings.json</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Encryption in transit</strong>: HTTPS everywhere (HSTS), TLS to Azure services, STARTTLS to SMTP, TLS to MySQL if the connection string asks for it.</li>
        <li><strong>Encryption at rest</strong>: provided by the platforms (Azure Storage and Key Vault encrypt by default; the database depends on the host). The app itself encrypts only <em>URL/form IDs and email tokens</em>; it does not encrypt database columns. See <a href="/docs/system/data#encryption">Data &amp; encryption</a>.</li>
    </ul>
